Generated-frame quality options, each behind its own [ofxr] key, all 0 by default (every composition then byte for byte as
before: the NVIDIA occlusion fixtures' 112 output hashes against the build without this patch). Read at the session's
start and followed live (0066's watcher: LiveFlow / Snapshot fg_quality, kLiveFgQuality), without a rebuild: they are shader
bits (UseGameMotion 16-20 of the NVIDIA compositions, D3D12FrameSynthesizer::quality_bits, read per pair;
set_fg_quality). Bit 17 says the frames are read linear (an sRGB view: the periphery or a composed swapchain; Quad
Views' focus layer is UNORM and holds encoded values). NVIDIA path only.
  dcs_motion_sky_occlusion  MV path, a sky pixel whose samples differ by more than 25 % of the brighter (linear light),
                            where the two frames do not agree at the pixel itself and a G-buffer surface is found around
                            it (rings 1, 3, 6, 12 cells): the surface's own composition where its vector's fixed point
                            holds here, else the frame whose end the class atlas calls sky. The sky's colour check on
                            encoded values. HUD, labels, smoke and contrails (not in the G-buffer) are never forced.
                            Night ghost: trailing copy 6.3-11.1 -> 0.02-0.08 MAE.
  dcs_motion_hud_guard      MV path, a sky gather on a linear-read image: the samples' agreement and 0057's still-content
                            guard on encoded values (as on a UNORM image). HUD over a dark rolling sky (sRGB view) 14.8 ->
                            0.76 MAE; surfaces keep the linear-light check (thin wires unchanged).
  nvidia_edge_choice        where the four flow vectors spread over 1.5 px and the frames differ at the pixel, the one of
                            them or their mix whose ends agree best (skips 0030's fixed point when a grid vector is taken).
  dcs_motion_mask_band      the MVs also inside the cockpit mask where the class atlas says world at the pixel and at both
                            of the vector's ends, with the strict colour check on encoded values.
GPU (5424x5356 x2, 240 pairs, sRGB view): composition +1 us with the HUD guard, +5-7 us with all four; pack unchanged; no
new resource.

